Theorem RL-28: conservative RC flush for unknown callees

  Preconditions:
    - RL-28 governs unknown-callee barriers per Annex E §AIMS Selective
      Barriers: "Unknown callees (FFI, indirect, no contract) require a
      conservative flush of all pending RC ops."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - An unknown callee has no MemoryContract, so its effect on any variable's
      RC count is unknown (TF-5 CONSERVATIVE / IC-8a address-taken).

  Soundness property:
    Forall call site whose callee has no contract (FFI / ApplyIndirect /
    no-contract Apply):

      (P1) Flush decision: RL-28 conservatively flushes ALL pending RC ops at
           the call site.

      (P2) Soundness: with no contract, the callee may inc, dec, or share ANY
           reachable variable; flushing all pending RC ops ensures the count
           is materialized correctly before the unknown effect. Skipping the
           flush could leave the count stale across the unknown call.

    RL-28 is the safety fallback of RL-27: where RL-27's per-parameter
    selectivity needs a contract, RL-28 flushes unconditionally when none
    exists.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — unknown-callee flush:
      ffi_no_contract / indirect_no_contract / apply_no_contract -> flush all;
      known_contract_selective -> RL-27 selective (not all-flush).
      Coverage gate: 4 callee-shape cases. Negative-direction witness: an
      unknown (no-contract) callee must conservatively flush all pending RC
      ops — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl28_unknown_callee_flush;
        unknown-callee enumeration; emits Fail when an unknown callee skips
        the flush)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-28 via the unknown-callee enumeration (FFI / indirect / no-contract -> conservative all-flush; known-contract -> RL-27 selective) with a negative-direction witness confirming an unknown callee never skips the flush
